# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# worktrees live beside the repo, but never inside it
.worktrees/

# editors and operating systems
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# a ledger is written where the work is, and is never part of it. §7.6 gives a
# store no garbage collection, so one that gets committed only ever grows.
.nether/

# nothing generated belongs here except the site, which is committed on purpose

# Built by `scripts/task wasm`, not committed. A Rust release build is not
# byte-reproducible across machines, so a committed copy could only be checked
# by rebuilding it -- and then the committed copy is doing nothing. What is
# checked instead is the module the build produces: its exports, and its
# compressed size against `.wasm-ceiling`.
web/necropolis/nether.wasm

# site/font.py imports site/gfx.py to draw the specimen, and Python leaves
# these behind. One was committed before anyone noticed.
site/__pycache__/
